{"resourceIdentifier":"1036","resourceName":"Hillsborough County Waste to Energy (WtE) Facility 2009 Capital Expansion Unit 4","description":"The project consists of the installation of a new nominal 600 ton per day combustion unit (Unit #4) at the Hillsborough County Resource Recovery Facility (the Facility) located at 350 N. Falkenburg Road in Tampa, FL.  The Facility, and consequently the Project, is owned by Hillsborough County, Florida, and is operated on behalf of Hillsborough County (the County) by Covanta Hillsborough, Inc., a subsidiary of Covanta Energy, headquartered in Morristown, NJ.  Heat recovered from the combustion of municipal solid waste is used to generate electricity, which is predominately sold to Seminole Power.  Some power is also generated for the Countyï¿½s adjacent publically owned treatment works (POTW).  A new electrical tie-line is also currently under construction to supply electricity to a County water treatment facility.","location":{"latitude":27.952000,"longitude":-82.339800},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":null,"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1036"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"FL"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Hillsborough County"},{"type":"string","value":"Maharashtra, India"},{"type":"string","value":"+91 2425 225035"},{"type":"string","value":"malpani@malpani.com"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Late to verify"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"1036"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"35000"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Energy industries (renewable/non-renewable sources)"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"AM0025"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","val